Z||000000||88CoupeV6||11-28-2001||11:21 AM||||I love it. I don't ever remember it being so nice this time of year on the east coast. I hope we don't get hit hard later. I HATE THE SNOW. Sorry to those with snow I know how you feel. I have been buried in it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
Z||000001||turbo86se||11-28-2001||11:31 AM||||I hear ya Josh. It's almost December and we're still wearing shorts everyday. It's like 80 out, no humidity, got all the windows open. Think I'll take the T-Tops off the Fiero and go get some lunch!<P>If I could figure out the PIP, I'd show you a neat pic of my old Fiero BURIED in snow from '94 up in MD. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SC.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||11-28-2001||12:16 PM||||It has been a nice fall and start to winter so far (crossing fingers!)  We were up to it in snow by Nov 20 last year, and it really hasn't even gone below freezing this year!  Daytime temps in the 50' and 60's for the most part, nighttime into the 30's but no icey dew on the windows yet!<P>This may be the latest I have been able to drive my Fiero yet!  (It hibernates when the roads get covered in salt.)<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
